cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-flow-project: the Godot test project for the IDTX Flow extension"
abstract: >
  The Godot project that exercises datasource-flow. It holds no library code: it is
  scenes, USD fixtures and inspection scripts -- blendshape and morph stress tests,
  normals and skinning checks, unassigned-vertex cases -- with the rendered results
  committed beside them. An importer is judged by what comes out the far end, and a
  fixture with its output next to it is the only form of that claim a reader can check
  without running anything.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/datasource-flow-project"
keywords:
  - godot
  - usd
  - test-fixtures
  - regression-testing
references:

  - type: software
    title: "datasource-flow: IDTX Flow as a Godot extension"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/datasource-flow"
    notes: >
      The extension under test, vendored here as addons/IDTXFlow. This repository is
      that one's evidence, which is why they are separate: a fixture set that ships
      inside the thing it tests can be quietly adjusted to pass.

  - type: software
    title: "transport-godot-mcp: an in-editor MCP server for the Godot editor"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-godot-mcp"
    notes: >
      Vendored as addons/vsekai_godot_mcp, from its addon-root branch. It is how the
      inspection scripts are driven without a person clicking through the editor.

  - type: software
    title: "OpenUSD: Universal Scene Description"
    authors:
      - name: "Pixar Animation Studios"
    url: "https://openusd.org/"
    notes: "The .usda fixtures are USD; the format decides what the tests can express."
